    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d444">

                <pb facs="0424" n="416" sameAs="frus:frus1940v04/pg416"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.0146/813</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Lothian</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 392</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-08-09">August 9, 1940</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Under instructions from His Majesty’s
                    Principal Secretary of State for Foreign Affairs I have the honour to inform you
                    that His Majesty’s Government in the United Kingdom have decided to withdraw for
                    service elsewhere the military garrisons which they have hitherto maintained in
                    China at Shanghai, Peking and Tientsin.</p>
                <p>As regards the withdrawal of the troops from North China I have the honour to
                    inform you that His Majesty’s Government reserve all <pb facs="0425" n="417"
                        xml:id="pg417"/> their treaty rights under the Peking Protocol of September
                    7th, 1901,<anchor n="41" xml:id="d444-f1"/> until such time as the said Protocol
                    has been amended or abrogated by agreement between the Powers concerned.<anchor
                        n="42" xml:id="d444-f2"/></p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lothian</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d444-f1" n="41" xml:id="d444-f1-content">
                <p><ref target="frus1901#pg_312"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>,
                        1901, Appendix (Affairs in China), p. 312</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d444-f2" n="42" xml:id="d444-f2-content">
                <p>The Acting Secretary of State acknowledged receipt of this British note in a note
                    dated August 13.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
